---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
import {
  systemDiagram,
  agentInteractionDiagram,
  hooksDiagram,
  commandsDiagram,
  scriptsDiagram,
  runtimeStateDiagram,
  safetyDiagram,
} from '../data/diagrams';
---

<DocsLayout title="How It Works" sectionLabel="Architecture" activeSlug="arch-visual">

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How VibeCrew Works</h2>
    <p>VibeCrew is a system of interlocking parts: a plugin shell, specialized agents, lifecycle hooks, slash commands, bash scripts, and per-project runtime state. Select a tab to see how each part fits together.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Tab navigation -->
  <div class="arch-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Architecture sections">
    <button class="arch-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-plugin" data-tab="plugin">Plugin Structure</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-agents" data-tab="agents">Sub-Agents</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-hooks" data-tab="hooks">Hooks</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-commands" data-tab="commands">Slash Commands</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-scripts" data-tab="scripts">Bash Scripts</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-runtime" data-tab="runtime">Runtime State</button>
    <button class="arch-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-safety" data-tab="safety">Permissions &amp; Safety</button>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Plugin Structure ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel active" id="panel-plugin" role="tabpanel">
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Plugin Structure</h3>
      <p>VibeCrew is a <strong>Claude Code plugin</strong> &mdash; an add-on that gives Claude Code new abilities. When you open a project with VibeCrew installed, Claude Code reads a manifest file and automatically loads agents, skills, hooks, scripts, MCP servers, and permissions. Everything lives inside the <code>claude-plugin-vibe-crew/</code> directory.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What it is</strong>
            <p>A self-contained folder with a <code>plugin.json</code> manifest that registers 14 agents, 33 slash commands, 16 hooks, ~80 scripts, and 9 MCP servers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem it solves</strong>
            <p>Without a plugin, you'd manually configure each agent, permission rule, and automation script for every project. The plugin bundles everything into a single install.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={systemDiagram} caption="Plugin components and how Claude Code loads them" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Sub-Agents ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-agents" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Sub-Agents</h3>
      <p>Instead of one AI doing everything, VibeCrew splits work across <strong>14 specialized agents</strong> &mdash; like a real development team with planners, builders, testers, and reviewers. Each agent runs a specific model (Opus for complex decisions, Haiku for fast mechanical tasks, Sonnet for documentation) and operates either inline or in an isolated worktree.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What they are</strong>
            <p>AI "specialists" with scoped tool access, model selection, and turn budgets. The Workflow Orchestrator routes work; the Builder writes code; the Verifier runs tests; the Performance Coach scores sessions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
            <p>A single AI context window fills up fast when researching, coding, and testing in one session. Worktree agents offload expensive research into isolated contexts &mdash; only the distilled output enters your main session, saving thousands of tokens.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="agent-legend">
      <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-accent)"></span> Opus (complex reasoning)</span>
      <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-amber)"></span> Haiku (fast tasks)</span>
      <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-blue)"></span> Sonnet (documentation)</span>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={agentInteractionDiagram} caption="Agent topology: how agents hand off work to each other" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Hooks ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-hooks" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Hooks</h3>
      <p>Hooks are <strong>automatic safety checks</strong> that run behind the scenes at zero token cost. When an agent tries to write a file or run a command, hooks intercept the action and validate it before it executes. Think of them as security guards at every door &mdash; they check permissions instantly using small bash scripts, not AI processing.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What they are</strong>
            <p>Bash scripts triggered by Claude Code lifecycle events (session start, before/after tool use, session end). They read a JSON payload from stdin and return exit code 0 (allow) or 2 (block).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
            <p>AI models can forget rules mid-session. Hooks enforce constraints deterministically &mdash; the phase gate blocks source code writes before the foundation is complete, the quality gate catches build errors, and the data protector blocks destructive commands. No token cost, no forgetting.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={hooksDiagram} caption="Hook events mapped to their enforcement scripts" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Slash Commands ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-commands" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Slash Commands</h3>
      <p>Slash commands are the <strong>primary user interface</strong> to VibeCrew. You type a command starting with <code>/</code> and the system handles the rest. Each command is defined as a <code>SKILL.md</code> file with YAML frontmatter (name, description, arguments) and a markdown body containing the full workflow: preconditions, steps, error handling, and agent handoffs.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What they are</strong>
            <p>33 commands across 7 categories: setup, planning, development, quality, safety, session management, and gamification. Some are script-only (zero token cost), others orchestrate multiple agents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
            <p>Without slash commands, you'd need to manually prompt the AI with detailed instructions for every workflow step. Commands encode expert workflows into one-word triggers &mdash; <code>/wrap</code> runs quality checks, scores your session, generates docs, and commits, all automatically.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={commandsDiagram} caption="How a slash command flows from user input to results" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Bash Scripts ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-scripts" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Bash Scripts</h3>
      <p>Scripts are the <strong>worker bees</strong> of VibeCrew &mdash; ~80 small bash programs that do the actual mechanical work. While agents think and make decisions, scripts create files, update project state, calculate scores, and send notifications. They run in milliseconds and always produce the same result for the same input.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What they are</strong>
            <p>Deterministic bash scripts organized by function: core lifecycle, feature management, quality scoring, project analysis, documentation, gamification, and state management. Agents never write state files directly &mdash; all mutations go through scripts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
            <p>AI token cost scales with complexity. By offloading mechanical tasks (JSON manipulation, git operations, file formatting) to scripts, VibeCrew keeps AI focused on decisions while scripts handle bookkeeping at zero token cost. Scripts also guarantee consistency &mdash; state mutations are atomic and predictable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={scriptsDiagram} caption="Script categories and who calls them" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Runtime State ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-runtime" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Runtime State</h3>
      <p>Every project using VibeCrew gets a <code>.vibecrew/</code> folder that stores all runtime state: project configuration, foundation progress, feature backlog, session logs, Vibe Scores, architecture diagrams, and cross-session handoffs. This folder is the system's memory &mdash; it persists between sessions and lets agents pick up exactly where the last one left off.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What it is</strong>
            <p>A directory of JSON files and sub-folders created by <code>/setup</code>. Core files: <code>config.json</code> (preferences), <code>state.json</code> (current phase), <code>backlog.json</code> (feature specs), <code>gamification.json</code> (progression). Sub-directories hold sessions, scores, signals, locks, and architecture diagrams.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem it solves</strong>
            <p>AI sessions are stateless &mdash; each new conversation starts from scratch. The <code>.vibecrew/</code> folder gives the system persistent memory: which features are done, what phase you're in, your quality trends, and even architectural diagrams that agents reference instead of re-deriving structure from code.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={runtimeStateDiagram} caption="Runtime state files and who reads/writes them" />
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════ Permissions & Safety ═══════ -->
  <div class="arch-panel" id="panel-safety" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h3>Permissions &amp; Safety</h3>
      <p>VibeCrew uses a <strong>defense-in-depth</strong> model with three layers of protection. Before any agent action reaches your filesystem, it passes through permission rules, hook guards, and quality gates. This means the AI can work productively without asking for permission every 5 seconds, while being physically unable to do anything destructive.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What it is</strong>
            <p>Three concentric safety layers: <code>settings.json</code> (66 allow rules, 22 deny rules), PreToolUse hook scripts (phase gate, path restrictions, destructive command blocking), and Stop hook quality gates (typecheck, lint, build, cost limits).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem it solves</strong>
            <p>AI agents can attempt risky actions &mdash; force-pushing, deleting files, running as root, or writing code before architecture is decided. VibeCrew blocks these deterministically with bash scripts, not by hoping the model remembers the rules.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="safety-columns">
      <div class="safety-card allowed">
        <h4>Allowed without prompts</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>File operations</strong> &mdash; Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep</li>
          <li><strong>npm scripts</strong> &mdash; test, lint, build, format, type-check</li>
          <li><strong>Git</strong> &mdash; status, log, diff, add, commit, checkout, branch, worktree, revert, tags</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub/GitLab CLI</strong> &mdash; PR create/list/view, pipeline view</li>
          <li><strong>Shell utilities</strong> &mdash; jq, cat, ls, wc, sort, head, tail, mkdir, cp, mv</li>
          <li><strong>Security audits</strong> &mdash; npm audit, pip audit, cargo audit, govulncheck</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="safety-card blocked">
        <h4>Always blocked</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Privilege escalation</strong> &mdash; <code>sudo</code>, <code>su</code>, <code>doas</code>, <code>pkexec</code></li>
          <li><strong>Force operations</strong> &mdash; <code>git push --force</code>, <code>git reset --hard</code>, <code>git clean -f</code></li>
          <li><strong>Destructive commands</strong> &mdash; <code>rm -rf /</code>, <code>rm -rf ~</code>, <code>chmod 777</code></li>
          <li><strong>System modifications</strong> &mdash; <code>npm install -g</code>, <code>kill -9</code>, <code>systemctl</code>, <code>crontab</code></li>
          <li><strong>Data destruction</strong> &mdash; <code>DROP TABLE</code>, <code>DELETE FROM</code> without WHERE (hook layer)</li>
          <li><strong>Path violations</strong> &mdash; writes outside project root, source code before foundation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MermaidDiagram chart={safetyDiagram} caption="Three-layer defense: permissions → hooks → quality gates" />
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  /* ──── Tab navigation ──── */
  .arch-tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .arch-tab {
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-bottom: -1px;
  }

  .arch-tab:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .arch-tab.active {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* ──── Tab panels ──── */
  .arch-panel {
    display: none;
    animation: panelFadeIn 0.2s ease;
  }

  .arch-panel.active {
    display: block;
  }

  @keyframes panelFadeIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* ──── Panel intro ──── */
  .panel-intro {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .panel-intro h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .panel-intro > p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* ──── Key points ──── */
  .key-points {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .key-point {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .key-point strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .key-point p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .key-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .key-icon.purple {
    background: var(--color-accent-bg);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .key-icon.green {
    background: var(--color-green-dim);
    color: var(--color-green);
  }

  /* ──── Agent legend ──── */
  .agent-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .legend-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legend-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* ──── Safety columns ──── */
  .safety-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .safety-card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .safety-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .safety-card ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .safety-card li {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .safety-card li code {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .safety-card.allowed {
    border-color: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.2);
  }

  .safety-card.allowed h4 {
    color: var(--color-green);
  }

  .safety-card.blocked {
    border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.2);
  }

  .safety-card.blocked h4 {
    color: var(--color-red);
  }

  /* ──── Responsive ──── */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .arch-tabs {
      gap: 0;
    }

    .arch-tab {
      padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
    }

    .key-points {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .safety-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function() {
    var tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.arch-tab');
    var panels = document.querySelectorAll('.arch-panel');
    // Track which panels have had mermaid rendered
    var rendered = { plugin: true }; // first panel renders on load

    function switchTab(target) {
      // Update tabs
      tabs.forEach(function(t) {
        t.classList.remove('active');
        t.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
      });
      var activeTab = document.querySelector('[data-tab="' + target + '"]');
      if (activeTab) {
        activeTab.classList.add('active');
        activeTab.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');
      }

      // Update panels
      panels.forEach(function(p) {
        p.classList.remove('active');
        p.hidden = true;
      });
      var panel = document.getElementById('panel-' + target);
      if (panel) {
        panel.classList.add('active');
        panel.hidden = false;

        // Render mermaid diagrams on first show (hidden elements have 0 width)
        if (!rendered[target] && window.mermaid) {
          rendered[target] = true;
          // Small delay to let the browser paint the visible panel
          requestAnimationFrame(function() {
            var nodes = panel.querySelectorAll('.mermaid[data-processed]');
            if (nodes.length > 0) {
              // Already processed but at 0 width — re-render
              nodes.forEach(function(n) { n.removeAttribute('data-processed'); });
              mermaid.run({ nodes: nodes });
            } else {
              var pres = panel.querySelectorAll('pre.mermaid');
              if (pres.length > 0) {
                mermaid.run({ nodes: pres });
              }
            }
          });
        }
      }
    }

    tabs.forEach(function(tab) {
      tab.addEventListener('click', function() {
        switchTab(tab.getAttribute('data-tab'));
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
